nodes.body:
@slin1237 Could you review the request-admission approach here, or help identify the right reviewer? This addresses #41466 by rejecting the reported malformed native `/generate` inputs before streaming starts or requests reach the scheduler/detokenizer.

The PR records 512 passing CPU tests and 495 subtests, including production ASGI/admission-path regressions. Model execution and scheduler transport are replaced in those tests; real GPU process-survival validation remains unverified. Prior work and the scope of the consolidated validation are documented in the description.

The branch still needs updating for the minimum-base requirement in #21065 before fresh CI; `run-ci` is also missing. Feedback on the boundary and scope would be helpful, along with CI authorization after the branch update. Thanks!

